# Generic Silent Install Commands (MSI & EXE)

Standard one-liners for remote `SYSTEM` shells (ScreenConnect, NinjaOne, etc.) to install software from a local folder or direct URL without UAC prompts.

---

## 1. MSI Installers (CMD)

```cmd
:: Install from a local path
msiexec.exe /i "C:\Temp\installer.msi" /qn /norestart

:: Install directly from a URL
msiexec.exe /i "[https://example.com/installer.msi](https://example.com/installer.msi)" /qn /norestart

:: Download via curl, install silently, then delete the installer (best for redirects/proxies)
curl.exe -L "[https://example.com/installer.msi](https://example.com/installer.msi)" -o "C:\Windows\Temp\installer.msi" && msiexec.exe /i "C:\Windows\Temp\installer.msi" /qn /norestart && del "C:\Windows\Temp\installer.msi"

:: Install with verbose logging (for troubleshooting failed installs)
msiexec.exe /i "C:\Temp\installer.msi" /qn /norestart /l*v "C:\Windows\Temp\msi_install.log"
```

---

## 2. EXE Installers (CMD)

> Unlike MSI files, silent flags depend on how the vendor packaged the `.exe`. Use `start /wait ""` when chaining cleanup commands so CMD waits for the installer to finish before deleting it.

```cmd
:: Install from a local path (replace --quiet with the vendor's silent switch)
"C:\Temp\installer.exe" --quiet

:: Install from a local path and wait until completion
start /wait "" "C:\Temp\installer.exe" /S

:: Download via curl, install silently, wait, then delete the installer
curl.exe -L "[https://example.com/installer.exe](https://example.com/installer.exe)" -o "C:\Windows\Temp\installer.exe" && start /wait "" "C:\Windows\Temp\installer.exe" /S && del "C:\Windows\Temp\installer.exe"

:: Check supported switches on an unknown EXE (run interactively)
"C:\Temp\installer.exe" /?
```

### Common EXE Silent Switches

| Installer Type | Silent Switch | Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **NSIS** | `/S` | Case-sensitive (uppercase `S`) |
| **Inno Setup** | `/VERYSILENT /SUPPRESSMSGBOXES /NORESTART` | `/SILENT` shows progress bar |
| **InstallShield** | `/s /v"/qn"` | Passes `/qn` to wrapped MSI |
| **WiX / Burn** | `/quiet /norestart` | Common for Microsoft runtimes |
| **Custom / Modern** | `--quiet` or `--silent` | Used by tools like Sophos |

